         "description": "The vehicle control system must allow for stable trail braking by coordinating the steering angle sensor and acceleration pedal sensor. This coordination is essential to minimize understeer or oversteer during braking maneuvers."
      },  
      {  
         "ID": 19,  
         "description": "The brake system must be compatible with ABS (Anti-lock Braking System) interventions based on wheel speed data. This compatibility ensures effective deceleration and stability by preventing wheel lock-up during heavy braking."
      },  
      {  
         "ID": 47,  
         "description": "The system must include error correction algorithms to minimize any discrepancy in the steering feedback provided to the driver. These algorithms ensure that the steering input accurately reflects the vehicle's actual behavior, enhancing driver control and safety."
      }  
   ]
}

